!-----------------------------------------------------------------------
!
! Absorption cross-section NO3: NO3 + hv --> NO + O2
! Coupled reaction : NO3 + hv --> NO2 + O
! source : JPL-2006
! http://www.atmosphere.mpg.de/enid/2295
! -> Catalogue -> "Nitrogen Oxides" -> "NO3" -> "JPL-2006"
! Rem1: Quantum yield depends on the wl AND temperature.
!   i)  wl < 585nm: q.y. = 0.
!   ii) 585nm < wl < 640nm:
!       JPL-2006 reports table of q.y. vs. wl for T=190K, 230K, 298K
!       We then consider to interpolate linearly the q.y. by using data
!       given for temperatures bounding the actual temperature.
!       This interpolation is carried out in subroutine JRATES.
!   iii)wl > 640nm : q.y. = 0.
! Rem2: Temperature influence:
!   i) 172-220nm: T dep. according to the formula:
!           log10 crs = sum An*wl^n + (T-273)*sum Bn*wl^n
!       where An and Bn are parameters introduced in CRS_CFC.
!       The cross sections are computed in subroutine CRS_TDEP.
!   ii)220-235nm: T indep.
!       The cross sections have been obtained by extrapolation of Simon (1988)
!       at T=295K (see Ref.733, JPL-2006).
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Begins at wl interval :       115  | Finishes at wl interval :  166
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
!  no  from(nm) to(nm)  | crs (cm2) |   qyield(T=190k)  qyield(T=230k)   qyield(T=298k)
!-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
